# Copy to .env.local and fill in your key. .env.local is gitignored.
# The app reads these from the environment; the key is never sent through chat.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Optional — defaults to claude-opus-5-5. Use claude-haiku-5-5 for a faster demo.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5

# Remote MCP endpoint (/api/mcp), used when connecting from claude.ai web.
# Auth is the APP's responsibility (the framework is auth-agnostic). This example
# demonstrates two app-level modes:
#   MCP_OAUTH=1  → require OAuth 2.1 (PKCE) via the demo authorization server
#                  (app/oauth/* + /.well-known/*). What claude.ai web uses.
#   MCP_TOKEN=x  → simpler static bearer token (good behind a private tunnel).
# Leave both unset for an open endpoint (local dev only).
MCP_OAUTH=
MCP_TOKEN=
# claude.ai won't send tenant/user headers; pin them for the remote endpoint.
MCP_DEFAULT_TENANT=acme
MCP_DEFAULT_USER=web

# --- Consuming an EXTERNAL MCP server (inbound tools) -----------------------
# The assistant merges this app's own tools with tools from another MCP server
# (see server/mcp-tools.ts). By default it uses a zero-config in-process demo
# server (ext.weather.get, ext.time.now). Point the DEFAULT connector elsewhere:
#   EXTERNAL_MCP_URL  → a remote MCP server over Streamable HTTP
# EXTERNAL_MCP_URL=https://mcp.example.com/mcp
#   EXTERNAL_MCP_CMD  → a local MCP server over stdio (command to spawn)
# EXTERNAL_MCP_CMD=npx -y @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem /tmp
#
# You can also add connectors at runtime from the Assistant page ("+ Add
# connector"). If the server requires OAuth, the app runs the full OAuth 2.1
# flow (discovery + dynamic registration + PKCE) in a popup — see
# server/mcp-oauth.ts and app/mcp/callback. To try it against this app's OWN
# protected endpoint, run with MCP_OAUTH=1 and connect to /api/mcp.
